      "statement":"For a covered UCITS fund's post-authorisation material change in an investment objective, policy or restriction, prior SFC approval is no longer required under this measure from 2025-11-28 if the change complies with home jurisdiction requirements, involves neither novel nor complex product features, and does not potentially have local policy implications. Covered funds are UCITS domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland or the Netherlands, and UK-domiciled schemes authorised as UK UCITS. If any product-feature or local-policy exception applies, or home requirements are not met, the circular does not remove the otherwise applicable approval requirement. An application received by the SFC before 2025-11-28 and still awaiting approval or authorisation at commencement remains subject to the existing approval or authorisation process; the new relief does not automatically dispose of it. The management company must still address applicable notifications and filings, and the SFC retains post-vetting, enquiry and regulatory-action powers. The actual approval outcome for an excluded or transitional case remains dependent on the existing rules and relevant FAQs, which are not supplied.",
